{
  "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
  "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (J. Craig Jett)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JETT: Our -- our first issue and our first contention is that Federal common law will govern the decision in this particular case, but we also have a due process point that we also believe is germane."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Jett, do I take it, from what you've just said, that you are recognizing this is a question of Federal common law and not due process, so that if Congress placed the burden on the defendant, there would be no constitutional infirmity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (J. Craig Jett)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JETT: We think that Congress could not under the -- the precedents of this Court and under the -- the basic common law construction that's fundamental, I think, to the -- to the criminal law in this -- in this country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (J. Craig Jett)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JETT: Well, we think that in -- that in every criminal case, with possibly the exception of -- of public welfare cases, that -- that there is an"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Which is the easier of the two cases for the defendant? A, the case where the argument is a burden of proof should be on -- on the -- the State as a due process matter or a common law matter in an insanity defense and, B, in a duress defense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I would think that it's easier in -- you know, we had -- we had a -- this term another case in which the argument is that you cannot have a separate insanity defense essentially and -- and exclude from the mens rea element of a crime the -- the lack of -- of mental capacity to -- to have that mens"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jett",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the -- but the judge does have a gatekeeping function in -- in a duress defense, so that a judge -- in any circumstance, if the judge decided that the evidence was insufficient to get to the jury, the judge can make that determination so that you have the trial court acting with the -- the -- to make sure that what the jury is going to hear is -- is an issue for which there is evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jett",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JETT: Congress has -- has never ruled on the duress defense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For three reasons, the burden of proving duress should be on the defendant, and the Government should not be required to disprove duress beyond a reasonable doubt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: How does self-defense fit into this equation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Of course, in the vast majority of criminal cases, there's no doubt that the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: The -- the Model Penal Code takes the position that every defense, affirmative defense, goes on the Government, and that's just a policy judgment --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is the test proposed by the Petitioner that -- that you have to prove non-duress by beyond a reasonable doubt?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2005-05-7053",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7aa288736e8ae434a9a02ff9bb942a6521a4a0cdebc1830b952c79df342c939b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7aa288736e8a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: No. More likely than not, the preponderance of the evidence standard."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
